    "result_text": "Done. Tests are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nI agreed with the finding and addressed it. The `-<n>` suffix is a structural element of the `customerCode` format, and the codebase's consistent design has format rules live in the `Owner*` helpers while function steps only orchestrate.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`OwnerCustomerCode`** \u2014 added `withSuffix(String base, int n)` next to `of` and `regionOf`, so this class remains the single authority that knows how a `customerCode` is spelled. Its javadoc notes the `REGION` prefix is untouched, so `regionOf`'s first-`-` assumption still holds.\n- **`DeduplicateCustomerCode`** \u2014 now calls `OwnerCustomerCode.withSuffix(base, n)` instead of building `base + \"-\" + n` inline. The step keeps only the orchestration concern (gather existing codes, find the smallest free `n`, set the result), and its javadoc now points at the format owner.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged \u2014 distinct owners still get distinct codes, and a collision still yields the smallest `-<n>` with `n \u2265 2`.",
