    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new step is wired correctly and follows the pipeline conventions well \u2014 `service(@Val Owner, OwnerRepository)` matches its siblings, `govern: [ transaction ]` is applied consistently, placement before `assignMembershipNumber` is right, and the `findAll()` scan mirrors `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`. The problem is where the *format knowledge* lives.\n\n**Finding: the `-<n>` suffix format rule is embedded in the step instead of in `OwnerCustomerCode`, the documented single source of truth for the customerCode format.**\n\n`OwnerCustomerCode` is explicitly designed as the one authority for the `customerCode` shape. Its javadoc: *\"Single source of truth for an owner's customerCode ... It owns both sides of the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format so the write-time side (`AssignCustomerCode`, which constructs it) and the read-time side (`OwnerMapper.locality`, which recovers the region from it) cannot drift.\"* It even exposes `regionOf(...)` for parsing the format back out. `AssignCustomerCode.service` holds no format logic at all \u2014 it delegates to `OwnerCustomerCode.of(owner)`. The same delegation pattern holds across `OwnerIdentity`, `OwnerHousehold`, `OwnerTelephone`, `OwnerLocality`: format rules live in the `Owner*` helpers, and the function steps only orchestrate.\n\n`DeduplicateCustomerCode` breaks that by introducing a brand-new structural element of the code \u2014 the `base + \"-\" + n` suffix \u2014 entirely inside a pipeline step. `OwnerCustomerCode` now no longer owns \"both sides\" of the format: a third author produces customerCode values it doesn't know about. This is exactly the drift the codebase's design works to prevent (e.g. if anyone later needs to strip or recognise a dedup suffix, or if `regionOf`'s first-`-` assumption ever needs to account for the suffix, the knowledge isn't where every other part of the code looks for it).\n\n**Suggested change:** move the suffix construction into `OwnerCustomerCode` (e.g. a `withSuffix(String base, int n)` / `dedupedVariant(...)` method, next to `of`/`regionOf`), and have the step call it. The step keeps only the orchestration concern \u2014 gather existing codes, find the smallest free `n`, set the result \u2014 while the format authority stays the single place that knows how a customerCode is spelled.\n\nMinor, non-blocking: the class javadoc is thorough and matches the house style; no change needed there.",
